{"key":"eris","name":"Eris","accent":"#3dffd0","based":"Mesa/Boogie JP-2C (John Petrucci)","intro":"Eris is new: a compact, matte-black head shaped like the JP-2C. The cabinet's top front is cut away at a steep slant (about 55 degrees), and that slanted face is one sheet of black mesh framed by the cabinet edges, so the frame slants with it. Below it is a short, flat control panel with a solid-state look: no tubes, tick-mark dials, a thin teal light. CHANNEL picks the three JP-2C channels, VOICE steps through the captured settings on that channel, and BOOST adds the TS808 or Shred versions.","notes":["Channel 1: clean at gain 6 and gain 10. Gain blends between them.","Channel 3 voices: Lead (gain 6, 8 and 10, blended by Gain), Scooped lead (gain 8 and 10), JP lead, Ultimate lead, and Petrucci's current settings.","BOOST swaps to the matching TS808 or Shred capture on the Lead, Scooped lead and JP lead voices. Voices without a boosted capture stay as they are, and your pedal section can add the boost instead.","Not used on the panel: the power-amp-only captures (useful later for Eidolon), two EQ variants, and the five old TS808 captures the pack itself marks as bad. The power-amp-only files are JP2C Capture 20 Power Amp Only No EQ - Emil Rohbe and JP2C Capture 21 Power Amp Only With EQ - Emil Rohbe."],"W":1774,"H":678,"skins":[{"id":"eris","ptrOff":false}],"knobs":[{"label":"Gain","b":[159,410,97,97],"o":[50.227,50.32],"c":[207.7,458.8],"r":38.7,"v":0.75},{"label":"Treble","b":[347,410,97,97],"o":[50.289,50.32],"c":[395.8,458.8],"r":38.7,"v":0.6},{"label":"Middle","b":[535,410,97,97],"o":[50.351,50.32],"c":[583.8,458.8],"r":38.7,"v":0.35},{"label":"Bass","b":[723,410,97,97],"o":[50.423,50.32],"c":[771.9,458.8],"r":38.7,"v":0.45},{"label":"Presence","b":[911,410,97,97],"o":[50.485,50.32],"c":[960.0,458.8],"r":38.7,"v":0.55},{"label":"Master","b":[1100,410,97,97],"o":[49.526,50.32],"c":[1148.0,458.8],"r":38.7,"v":0.45},{"label":"Output","b":[1288,410,97,97],"o":[49.588